                <pb facs="0523" n="429" xml:id="pg429"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.124a/95: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reber</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-17T14:00:00-00:44">September 17, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>122. Department’s telegram No. 70, August 21, 4 p.m. Dr. Smith sails tomorrow to
                    visit neighboring countries as instructed. He expects to be absent about 23
                    days.</p>
                <p>The President said to him yesterday that when arrangements providing for a more
                    permanent medical adviser were concluded, he hoped that Dr. Smith would remain
                    for another period.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reber</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
